From: rstmcsoch <300077786+rstmcsoch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 03:44:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(admin): complete Admin Panel control over every
messaging feature

Every user-facing messaging behaviour now has an Admin Panel control, and
every control is enforced on the server as well as in the UI.

Availability switches (Features, reusing the existing rollout editor):
messages        global direct-message switch (already existed)
messageDeletion unsend control + the delete_message API action
messageSearch   conversation search + the messages_search query
readReceipts    the seen marker + the read_messages action
emojiPicker     the composer's emoji control

Global limits (Communications -> Messaging limits, stored in app_settings
through the existing validateSetting registry):
messages.maxLength          1-4000 characters, default 2000
messages.rateWindowSeconds  0-86400, 0 disables the quota
messages.rateMaxMessages    1-1000 sends inside the window

Per-account restrictions (Communications -> Message restrictions):
admin_message_restrictions adds send_disabled, receive_disabled and
suspended_until on top of the existing admin_message_controls switch.
Registered as migration 3 with CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS so an existing
deployment takes the upgrade and a fresh one pays nothing.

Server enforcement lives in lib/messaging-policy.ts and app/api/social:
the length ceiling, the sliding-window send quota, and the per-account
restriction verdict are all resolved per request. The previous
admin_message_controls lookup used PostgreSQL array syntax that libSQL
cannot parse, so the global DM switch was never actually enforced on the
deployed runtime; it now runs through the same code path.

Client mirroring: the composer honours the configured length, and the
delete, search, emoji and seen controls are removed from the DOM when their
switch is off rather than hidden with CSS.

Analytics reports messages sent, active conversations and the current
restriction counts; the Users detail page shows an account's messaging
state read-only, pointing at Communications for changes.

tests/admin-messaging.test.ts drives the real admin functions and the real
public API against a real libSQL database with real signed-in accounts:
persistence, audit, authorization, validation, the API chain for every
switch and limit, a forged client flag, and migration replay.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
