From 835304116d59625979be572c8e863d2d9728ba9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rstmcsoch <300077786+rstmcsoch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 03:52:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(admin): let private accounts be limited to their
existing followers

The audit brief calls for a non-follower messaging restriction where the
relationship model exists, and FunctionGram already has one: the follows
table. The switch is off by default, so today's behaviour (anyone may
message a private profile) is unchanged until an administrator turns it on.

Enforced in the message action after the per-account restrictions, and it
reuses the follow graph rather than introducing a second relationship
model. Notes to oneself are never gated. A malformed stored value falls
back to off, so it can never open the gate.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
